---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Features2 from '~/components/widgets/Features2.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Product Description Writing Services | Top League',
  description:
    'Persuasive, research-driven and SEO-friendly product descriptions that help shoppers understand your products and feel confident buying them.',
};
---

<!-- /*___________________________________🟢 ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ 🟢 ___________________________________*/ -->
<!-- //THIS IS A CUSTOM BODY CLASS CODE 🔴🟢🔴🟢🔴🟢🔴🟢🔴🟢 -->

<Layout metadata={metadata} pageClass="product-description-page">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="eyebrow">
        <span class="dot"></span>
        Product description writing
      </div>

      <h1>
        Product descriptions
        <span>that make buying easier.</span>
      </h1>

      <p>
        We turn product features into meaningful reasons to buy, with persuasive,
        research-driven and SEO-friendly product descriptions.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href="#contact">Request a free sample</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="#why">See what's included</a>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-note">
        No obligation. Just good product writing for you to evaluate.
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

<!-- /*___________________________________🟢 ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ 🟢 ___________________________________*/ -->
<!-- THE IDEA // WHY IT MATTERS --> <!-- 4. What is coming: three cards -->

  <Features2
    id="coming"
    classes={{container: 'coming-section', headline: {container: 'max-w-3xl !mx-0 !text-left',},}}// THIS IS A CUSTOM CLASS CODE 🔴🟢🔴🟢🔴🟢🔴🟢🔴🟢     
    tagline="Why it matters"
    title="Good product descriptions make the value obvious."
    subtitle="The right words connect what a product does with what a customer actually cares about."
    columns={3}
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Features need meaning',
        description:
          'Features tell shoppers what a product has. Benefits help them understand what it can do for them. We bring the two together through clear, compelling writing.',
        icon: 'tabler:rocket',
      },
      {
        title: 'Buyers need answers',
        description:
          'We consider your target audience, their priorities and the questions they’re likely to ask before putting words on the page.',
        icon: 'tabler:calendar-event',
      },
      {
        title: 'Products need visibility',
        description:
          'We incorporate relevant search keywords naturally, without compromising readability or turning your descriptions into keyword lists.',
        icon: 'tabler:gift',
      },
    ]}
  />

<!-- /*___________________________________🟢 ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ 🟢 ___________________________________*/ -->

<!-- 01 // FAMILIAR SHOPPING MOMENT --> <!-- 3. What is coming: three cards --> <!-- THE SHOPPING MOMENT -->

<section class="section band" id="story">
  <div class="container intro">

    <aside>
      <div class="kicker">A familiar shopping moment</div>
      <div class="num" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
    </aside>

    <div class="intro-copy">
      <h2>Someone is interested in your product. But are they convinced?</h2>

      <p>Imagine someone browsing your online store.</p>

      <p>They find a product that looks promising. The photographs are appealing. The price seems reasonable. They scroll down to learn a little more.</p>

      <p>And then they find a description that tells them almost nothing.</p>

      <p>A list of specifications. A few generic sentences. Perhaps some technical details copied straight from the manufacturer’s catalogue.</p>

      <p>The shopper still has questions. Will it solve their problem? Is it worth the price? What makes it different from the dozens of alternatives available online?</p>

      <p>They hesitate. They open another tab. And your product becomes just another option they considered.</p>

      <p><strong>The problem isn’t necessarily your product. Sometimes, it’s the way your product is presented.</strong></p>

      <p>A good product description closes that gap. It helps shoppers understand what they’re looking at, imagine how it fits into their lives and recognise why it might be the right choice.</p>

      <p>That’s what we believe product writing should accomplish.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- /*___________________________________🟢 ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ 🟢 ___________________________________*/ -->

<!-- THE TOP LEAGUE APPROACH -->
<section class="section" id="difference">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="feature-head">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">The Top League approach</div>
        <h2>Your product may be excellent. Your description should make that obvious.</h2>
        <p>Effective product copy doesn’t need to be complicated. It needs to communicate the right things in the right way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="features">
      <article class="feature">
        <div class="kicker">× THE USUAL WAY</div>
        <h3>Descriptions that get in the way</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Long lists of unexplained specifications</li>
          <li>Generic claims that could describe any product</li>
          <li>Keyword-heavy sentences that are hard to read</li>
          <li>Pushy language and exaggerated promises</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="feature">
        <div class="kicker">✓ THE TOP LEAGUE APPROACH</div>
        <h3>Copy that helps customers decide</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Clear information that answers real questions</li>
          <li>Meaningful benefits connected to product features</li>
          <li>Natural keywords and readable copy</li>
          <li>Persuasion grounded in the product’s actual value</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- /*___________________________________🟢 ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ 🟢 ___________________________________*/ -->
<!-- HOW WE WORK -->
<section class="section band" id="process">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="feature-head">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">How we work</div>
        <h2>Before we write about your product, we need to understand it.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Good product descriptions don’t begin with a writing template.
        They begin with understanding.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="process">
      <article>
        <div class="num">STEP 01</div>
        <h3>Understand the product</h3>
        <p>We examine its features, specifications, intended uses and distinguishing qualities. We identify what a prospective customer needs to know.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="num">STEP 02</div>
        <h3>Understand the buyer</h3>
        <p>Who is likely to purchase this product? What matters to them? What concerns might prevent them from buying?</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="num">STEP 03</div>
        <h3>Find the right words</h3>
        <p>We identify relevant keywords and translate product information into clear, benefit-oriented language.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="num">STEP 04</div>
        <h3>Write, review and refine</h3>
        <p>We review the copy for clarity, accuracy, readability and SEO considerations before delivery.</p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
  
</Layout>
